※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4370
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4370 LANG_RELRO_NOT_MUT

※ `@[relro]` stands on a variable defined `mut`.  One without it is written by
※ nothing at all and is in the read-only data from the start, so the attribute
※ would say less than the definition already does.
※
※ Compare: **C**, where `const` and a section of one's own are two separate
※ things and nothing says when one of them is redundant; **D**, where
※ `immutable` alone is the rule and there is no second word to get wrong.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[relro]
let limit: u32 = 10u32

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    ⎕narrow(limit, ⌜u6⌝) ?? 0u6
